(65, 1, 5, '10', '40min-50min', 'none', '<ul><li kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 20px;=\"\" font-weight:=\"\" 600;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;=\"\" text-align:=\"\" start;=\"\" background-color:=\"\" rgb(19,=\"\" 20,=\"\" 28);\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 30px; color: rgb(238, 156, 19);\">Beginner level is split into four modules. The following lessons will be covered in this level .Brief history and origin of Carnatic music.</li></ul><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Differentiating between Carnatic and Hindustani music.</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Understanding the basic svaras (sa, ri, ga, ma, pa, dha, ni).</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Introduction to the concept of octaves (mandra, madhya, and taara saptak).</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Practice basic note patterns in different speeds.</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Emphasis on precision in pitch and timing.</span></p>', 1, 3, NULL, '2023-12-05 11:04:54', NULL),
(66, 1, 2, '20', '40min-50min', 'none', '<ul><li style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 30px; margin-left: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(238, 156, 19); font-family: \" kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 20px;=\"\" font-weight:=\"\" 600;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;=\"\" text-align:=\"\" start;=\"\" background-color:=\"\" rgb(19,=\"\" 20,=\"\" 28);\"=\"\">Beginner level is split into four modules. The following lessons will be covered in this level .Brief history and origin of Carnatic music.</li></ul><p style=\"text-align: left; margin-bottom: 23px; position: relative; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: \" kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Differentiating between Carnatic and Hindustani music.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: left; margin-bottom: 23px; position: relative; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: \" kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Understanding the basic svaras (sa, ri, ga, ma, pa, dha, ni).</span></p><p style=\"text-align: left; margin-bottom: 23px; position: relative; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: \" kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Introduction to the concept of octaves (mandra, madhya, and taara saptak).</span></p><p style=\"text-align: left; margin-bottom: 23px; position: relative; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: \" kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Practice basic note patterns in different speeds.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: left; margin-bottom: 23px; position: relative; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: \" kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Emphasis on precision in pitch and timing.</span></p>', 1, 3, NULL, '2023-12-05 11:04:54', NULL),
(67, 1, 3, '15', '40min-50min', 'none', '<ul><li kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 20px;=\"\" font-weight:=\"\" 600;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;=\"\" text-align:=\"\" start;=\"\" background-color:=\"\" rgb(19,=\"\" 20,=\"\" 28);\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 30px; color: rgb(238, 156, 19);\">Beginner level is split into four modules. The following lessons will be covered in this level .Brief history and origin of Carnatic music.</li></ul><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Differentiating between Carnatic and Hindustani music.</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Understanding the basic svaras (sa, ri, ga, ma, pa, dha, ni).</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Introduction to the concept of octaves (mandra, madhya, and taara saptak).</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Practice basic note patterns in different speeds.</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Emphasis on precision in pitch and timing.</span></p>', 1, 3, NULL, '2023-12-05 11:04:54', NULL),
(68, 1, 4, '15', '40min-50min', 'nane', '<ul><li kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 20px;=\"\" font-weight:=\"\" 600;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;=\"\" text-align:=\"\" start;=\"\" background-color:=\"\" rgb(19,=\"\" 20,=\"\" 28);\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 30px; color: rgb(238, 156, 19);\">Beginner level is split into four modules. The following lessons will be covered in this level .Brief history and origin of Carnatic music.Differentiating between Carnatic and Hindustani music.</li></ul><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Understanding the basic svaras (sa, ri, ga, ma, pa, dha, ni).</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Introduction to the concept of octaves (mandra, madhya, and taara saptak).</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Practice basic note patterns in different speeds.</span></p><p kumbh=\"\" sans\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 18px;=\"\" line-height:=\"\" unset;\"=\"\" style=\"margin-bottom: 23px; text-align: left; position: relative;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Emphasis on precision in pitch and timing.</span></p>', 1, 3, NULL, '2023-12-05 11:04:54', NULL),
(177, 5, 5, 'none', '30-40 mins', '10', '<div>This level is split into four modules. The following concepts will be covered in this level:</div><div><br></div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to Carnatic Music&nbsp;</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Detailed exercises to strengthen the foundation</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to the different types of Talams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Concept of Melakarta Ragam</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Geethams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Nottuswarams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Swarajathi</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Lakshana Geethams</div><div><br></div>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-01-18 13:28:49', NULL),
(178, 5, 2, 'none', '40-45 mins', '20', '<div><div>In this level the following concepts will be covered:</div><div><br></div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Varnams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Kritis</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to new Ragams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Singing in different kalams/speed.</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Brushing up the foundation lessons in various ragams.</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to the new concept of Raga Sancharam and Manodharmam</div></div><div><br></div>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-01-18 13:28:49', NULL),
(179, 5, 3, 'none', '45-55 mins', '10', '<div>In this level the following concepts will be covered:</div><div><br></div><div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Complex Varnams and Kritis</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Complex Group kritis and Swarajatis of several composers</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Compositions in complex talams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Exploring Manodharmam</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to conceptual ragams</div></div>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-01-18 13:28:49', NULL),
(180, 5, 4, 'none', '50-60 mins', '10', '<div><div>In this level the following concepts will be covered:</div><div><br></div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Focus on special requests solicited by the students</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Central focus on manodharmam/improvisational rendering</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Vision to construe aspects of the learnt compositions in a new dimension.&nbsp;</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Exploration of conceptual ragams</div></div>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-01-18 13:28:49', NULL),
(197, 9, 5, 'NA', '30-40 mins', '10', '<p>This level will be split into three modules. The following concepts will be covered at this level:</p><ul><li>Introduction to Cine Music</li><li>Step by step assistance in swara delineation</li><li>Introduction&nbsp; to frequencies/Swara position</li><li>Assistance to singing in beat and Off-beat</li><li>Finding your scale</li><li>Ear training</li><li>Simple Vocal exercises</li><li>Assistance to expansion of vocal range</li></ul>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-01-22 13:49:09', NULL),
(198, 9, 2, 'CLF-1', '40-45 mins', '10', '<p>This level is split into three modules. The following concepts will be covered in this level.</p><ul><li>Introduction to new songs</li><li>Step by step assistance in swara delineation</li><li>Breath control exercises</li><li>Difference between singing classical and non-classical</li><li>Introduction to Dynamics and Modulation</li><li>Focus on Voice culture</li><li>Intermediate Ear Training</li></ul>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-01-22 13:49:09', NULL),
(199, 9, 3, 'CLF-2', '45-55 mins', '10', '<p>This level will be split into three modules. The following concepts will be covered in this level:</p><ul><li>Introduction to complex songs</li><li>Step by step assistance in swara delineation</li><li>Vocal Warm-ups</li><li>Focus on clean sustenance of notes and vocal health</li><li>Detailed exercises on lower octaves</li><li>Introduction to different ways of singing phrases﻿</li></ul>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-01-22 13:49:09', NULL),
(200, 9, 4, 'CLF-3', '50-60 mins', '10', '<p>This level will be split into three modules. The following concepts will be covered in this level:</p><ul><li>Introduction to intricate songs</li><li>Step by step assistance in swara delineation</li><li>Understanding difference between Scale and Key of a song</li><li>Introduction to the concept of major scale and minor scale</li><li>Assistance on maintaining tonal balance</li><li>Focus on requests solicited by the student</li><li>Focus on Vibrato, vocal expression, vocal registers and their uses</li><li>Assisstance to singing in the right posture</li><li>Detailed review of all the above learnt concepts</li></ul>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-01-22 13:49:09', NULL),
(205, 21, 5, '10', '30-40 mins', '-', '', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-05 14:26:43', NULL),
(206, 21, 2, '10', '40-45 mins', 'CLF-1', '', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-05 14:26:43', NULL),
(207, 21, 3, '10', '45-55 mins', 'CLF-2', '', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-05 14:26:43', NULL),
(208, 21, 4, '10', '50-60 mins', 'CLF-3', '', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-05 14:26:43', NULL),
(209, 15, 5, '10', '30-40 mins', '-', '<div>This level is split into four modules. The following concepts will be covered in this level:</div><div><br></div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to Carnatic Music&nbsp;</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Detailed exercises to strengthen the foundation</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to the different types of Talams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Concept of Melakarta Ragam</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Geethams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Nottuswarams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Swarajathi</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Lakshana Geethams</div>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-13 06:01:03', NULL),
(210, 15, 2, '10', '40-45 mins', 'CLF-1', '<div><div>In this level the following concepts will be covered:</div><div><br></div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Varnams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Kritis</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to new Ragams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Singing in different kalams/speed.</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Brushing up the foundation lessons in various ragams.</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to the new concept of Raga Sancharam and Manodharmam</div></div>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-13 06:01:03', NULL),
(211, 15, 3, '10', '45-55 mins', 'CLF-2', '<div>In this level the following concepts will be covered:</div><div><br></div><div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Complex Varnams and Kritis</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Complex Group kritis and Swarajatis of several composers</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Compositions in complex talams</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Exploring Manodharmam</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Introduction to conceptual ragams</div></div>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-13 06:01:03', NULL),
(212, 15, 4, '10', '50-60 mins', 'CLF-3', '<div>In this level the following concepts will be covered:</div><div><br></div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Focus on special requests solicited by the students</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Central focus on manodharmam/improvisational rendering</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Vision to construe aspects of the learnt compositions in a new dimension.&nbsp;</div><div>•⁠&nbsp; ⁠Exploration of conceptual ragams</div>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-13 06:01:03', NULL),
(213, 16, 5, 'none', '30-40 mins.', '10', '<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b><u>Module 1: Getting Acquainted</u></b></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: \" source=\"\" sans=\"\" pro\",=\"\" -apple-system,=\"\" blinkmacsystemfont,=\"\" \"segoe=\"\" ui\",=\"\" roboto,=\"\" \"helvetica=\"\" neue\",=\"\" arial,=\"\" sans-serif,=\"\" \"apple=\"\" color=\"\" emoji\",=\"\" ui=\"\" symbol\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 1rem;\"=\"\">Understand the fundamentals of the guitar as an instrument</span><br></li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Introduction to basic musical notes</li></ul><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b><u>Module 2: Tuning Mastery</u></b></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: \" source=\"\" sans=\"\" pro\",=\"\" -apple-system,=\"\" blinkmacsystemfont,=\"\" \"segoe=\"\" ui\",=\"\" roboto,=\"\" \"helvetica=\"\" neue\",=\"\" arial,=\"\" sans-serif,=\"\" \"apple=\"\" color=\"\" emoji\",=\"\" ui=\"\" symbol\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 1rem;\"=\"\">Learn essential techniques for tuning the guitar</span><br></li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Develop ear training skills for accurate tuning</li></ul><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b><u>Module 3: String Exploration</u></b></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Dive into playing the 6th and 5th strings with confidence</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Master the techniques for playing the 4th and 3rd strings</li></ul><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b><u>Module 4: Song Introduction</u></b></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: \" source=\"\" sans=\"\" pro\",=\"\" -apple-system,=\"\" blinkmacsystemfont,=\"\" \"segoe=\"\" ui\",=\"\" roboto,=\"\" \"helvetica=\"\" neue\",=\"\" arial,=\"\" sans-serif,=\"\" \"apple=\"\" color=\"\" emoji\",=\"\" ui=\"\" symbol\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 1rem;\"=\"\">Explore exciting new songs to apply your skills</span><br></li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Conquer playing the 2nd and 1st strings for a complete guitar experience</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Unlock the potential of your guitar playing journey by enrolling in this comprehensive course!</li></ul>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-13 06:20:10', NULL),
(214, 16, 2, 'CLF-1', '40-45 mins.', '10', '', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-13 06:20:10', NULL),
(215, 16, 3, 'CLF-2', '45-50 mins.', '10', '', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-13 06:20:10', NULL),
(216, 16, 4, 'CLF-3', '50-60 mins.', '10', '', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-02-13 06:20:10', NULL),
(221, 10, 5, 'none', '30-40 mins', '10', '<ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Explore the components of a standard five-piece drum kit</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Gain detailed insights into drum kit anatomy</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Develop essential skills in reading drum notation</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Understand the language of drumming</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Introduction to the versatile Paradiddle concept</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Practical exercises to enhance drumming foundation</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Learn the art of Backbeats for rhythmic emphasis</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Explore Two Bar Patterns for dynamic drumming</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Introduction to the Hi-Hat Pedal and its applications</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Dive into complex exercises involving Hi-Hat, Snare, and Bass drum coordination</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Fine-tune drumming prowess with intricate exercises</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Master the art of Drum Fills for expressive playing</li></ul><div style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Enroll now and elevate your drumming journey with our comprehensive course!</span><br></div>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-03-06 05:46:30', NULL),
(222, 10, 2, 'CLF-1', '40-45 mins', '10', '<ul><li style=\"text-align: left; \">Learn to read musical symbols on a staff</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Introduction to essential drumming techniques: Flams, Drags, and Ruffs</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Master the Double Stroke Roll for increased dexterity</li><li style=\"text-align: left; \">Detailed exercises covering all four parts of the Drum Kit for understanding variations</li><li style=\"text-align: left; \">Explore diverse exercises focusing on various drumming variations</li><li style=\"text-align: left; \">Apply dotted notes in rudiments for added musical depth</li><li style=\"text-align: left; \">Understand the concept of \"Bounce\" for fluid drumming transitions</li><li style=\"text-align: left; \">Introduction to groove and fill-ins for rhythmic creativity</li><li style=\"text-align: left; \">Practical application of Time Signature in crafting dynamic grooves</li></ul><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Embark on your musical journey by enrolling in our course today!</span><br></p>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-03-06 05:46:30', NULL),
(223, 10, 3, 'CLF-2', '45-55 mins', '10', '<p style=\"text-align: left;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Learn to read musical symbols on a staff</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Introduction to essential drumming techniques: Flams, Drags, and Ruffs</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Master the Double Stroke Roll for increased dexterity</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Detailed exercises covering all four parts of the Drum Kit for understanding variations</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Explore diverse exercises focusing on various drumming variations</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Apply dotted notes in rudiments for added musical depth</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Understand the concept of \"Bounce\" for fluid drumming transitions</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Introduction to groove and fill-ins for rhythmic creativity</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Practical application of Time Signature in crafting dynamic grooves</li></ul><p style=\"text-align: left;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Embark on your musical journey by enrolling in our course today!<br></p>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-03-06 05:46:30', NULL),
(224, 10, 4, 'CLF-3', '50-60 mins', '10', '<br>', 1, 3, NULL, '2024-03-06 05:46:30', NULL);
